                <pb facs="1217" n="1105" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.922/59</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Siamese Legation to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>Referring to the Department of State’s memorandum dated June 21, 1934<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1066-f1"/> concerning the revision of Article III of the
                    Treaty between the United States and Siam signed at Washington, D. C., on the
                    16th December 1920,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1066-f2"/> Prince Damras, the Siamese
                    Minister, has now received instructions from Phya Phahol, State Councillor in
                    charge of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, to inform the Honorable Cordell Hull,
                    Secretary of State, that (1) the draft of the new Article III as set forth in
                    the aforesaid memorandum is acceptable to His Majesty’s Government; (2) the
                    Department of State’s proposal that the agreement revising this Article III
                    should be in the form of a supplementary treaty is quite agreeable; and (3)
                    Prince Damras is invested with full powers to conduct negotiations and to sign
                    the proposed supplementary treaty with the Representative of the Government of
                    the United States of America.</p>
                <p>The Siamese Minister will be very grateful to be informed when it will be
                    convenient for the Secretary of State to grant him an audience with a view to
                    ascertaining the pleasure of the United States Government as to the procedure
                    and date of signing the said supplementary treaty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-25">February 25,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
